  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Counter-Trafficking In Persons (C-TIP) Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This two-year project is an extension of the CTIP Activity implemented in Azerbaijan by IOM in partnership with USAID, since 2015. The project aims at preventing vulnerable populations from being trafficked, engaging in forced labor, and falling victim to gender-based violence, mainly manifested through domestic violence (GBV/DV). The proposed activities under this extension aim to build on the existing successes and deepen the partnership with the Government of Azerbaijan, civil society organizations (CSOs), and the private sector to increase dialogue and coordination for effective anti-trafficking and GBV/DV response. It also envisages increasing access to quality and equitable services and establishing a referral network of health, social welfare, CSOs, and law enforcement to address mental health of survivors and provide them with proper psychosocial services and assistance (MHPSS). The activity will continue strengthening CSOs and other service providers for improved services and legal aid for victims and potential victims of TIP, GBV/DV, raising public awareness, as well as supporting CSOs long-term strategic and financial sustainability. Beneficiaries affected by human trafficking and GBV/DV will be provided with economic opportunities to improve their welfare and reintegrate into society.</narrative>
  </description>
